[0m
[32m## Executive Summary  

[0m
[32mIGC Pharma, a for‑profit Maryland startup, is developing **MINT‑AD**, a digital health platform that stratifies Alzheimer’s‑disease (AD) risk and recommends personalized interventions. The company seeks **non‑dilutive** capital (grants) to fund product development, clinical validation, and hiring.  

[0m
[32mOur systematic search (see Section 2) identified **nine** currently open or imminently opening grant opportunities that satisfy the following criteria:  

[0m
[32m| Level | Funding Source | Program | Deadline (2026‑2027) | Award Range | Eligibility for IGC Pharma |
[0m
[32m|-------|----------------|---------|----------------------|-------------|----------------------------|
[0m
[32m| National | NIH/NIA SBIR (R41/R42) | Alzheimer’s‑Disease‑Focused SBIR | 5 Sept 2026 (FY 2027 receipt) | $250‑$700 k (Phase I) up to $3 M (Phase II) | Yes – U.S. for‑profit, <500 employees, SBIR‑eligible |
[0m
[32m| National | ARPA‑H SBIR | “Neuro‑Tech” FY 2027 | 1 Oct 2026 (receipt 5 Oct 2026) | $250‑$1 M (Phase I) | Yes – health‑tech, U.S.‑based |
[0m
[32m| National | FDA SBIR (Device) | Diagnostic Devices (AI‑Based) | 30 Oct 2026 (standard receipt) | $150‑$500 k (Phase I) | Yes – medical‑device classification possible |
[0m
[32m| National | CDC SBIR | Public‑Health Data Analytics | 15 Nov 2026 (standard receipt) | $150‑$400 k | Yes – data‑driven health tool |
[0m
[32m| National | NSF SBIR | Computational‑Science & AI | 5 Dec 2026 (standard receipt) | $250‑$600 k | Yes – AI‑driven analytics |
[0m
[32m| State | MII Technology‑Assessment (Quarterly) | $90‑$130 k (sole) / $180‑$130 k (joint) | 15 Oct 2026 (5 pm deadline) | $90‑$130 k (sole) | Yes – Maryland‑based, recent SBIR award required |
[0m
[32m| State | MII Company‑Formation (Bimonthly) | Up to $300 k (sole) / $180‑$430 k (joint) | 1 Nov 2026 (1st business day) | $300‑$430 k | Yes – licensed university tech (not required for MINT‑AD) |
[0m
[32m| State | Maryland SBIR/STTR Matching Fund (TEDCO) | Up to $25 k (Phase I) / $75 k (Phase II) | Rolling – submit via TEDCO portal | $25‑$75 k | Yes – must have recent federal SBIR/STTR award |
[0m
[32m| Sector | Alzheimer’s Association RWD Funding (2027 Cycle) | $100 k‑$1 M (12‑24 mo) | Projected 15 Jan 2027 (call announced) | $100‑$1 M | Yes – digital‑health data accepted |
[0m
[32m| Sector | Alzheimer’s Association Early‑Detection Grants | $150 k‑$500 k (2027) | Projected 1 Mar 2027 | $150‑$500 k | Yes – focus on early detection & risk stratification |

[0m
[32mAll nine opportunities are **open or will open** after the current date (14 Oct 2026). The remaining programs examined were either closed, required non‑eligible entity types (e.g., professional‑services firms), or demanded deliverables outside IGC Pharma’s scope (e.g., hardware‑only devices).  

[0m
[32mThe most strategically aligned opportunities are the **NIH/NIA SBIR (FY 2027)** and the **MII Technology‑Assessment award** (deadline 15 Oct 2026). Both provide sufficient funding magnitude and explicitly welcome AI‑driven health‑risk tools. The **Alzheimer’s Association RWD** grant is also a strong fit because it explicitly lists digital health technologies as eligible data sources.  

[0m
