[32m### 3.1 NIH/NIA Small‑Business Innovation Research (SBIR) – FY 2027  

[0m
[32m| Item | Detail |
[0m
[32m|------|--------|
[0m
[32m| **Program** | NIH/NIA SBIR – “Alzheimer’s Disease” topic (R41/R42) |
[0m
[32m| **Funder** | National Institute on Aging (NIA), part of NIH |
[0m
[32m| **URL** | <https://www.nia.nih.gov/research/sbir> |
[0m
[32m| **Deadline** | Standard receipt date **5 Sept 2026** for FY 2027 (applications accepted through the SBIR portal until that date) |
[0m
[32m| **Award Size** | Phase I: up to **$700,000** (2‑year) ; Phase II: up to **$3 million** (3‑year) |
[0m
[32m| **Eligibility** | U.S. for‑profit small business (<500 employees), must be SBIR‑eligible, no prior award restriction for first submission |
[0m
[32m| **Why it fits** | NIA explicitly funds “early detection, risk assessment, and prevention” technologies for AD (see “NIA SBIR funding ceilings” citation) and welcomes AI‑based risk models. |
[0m
[32m| **Red Flag** | Requires a **detailed research plan** and may expect a **clinical validation** component; IGC Pharma must demonstrate feasibility within 2 years. |
[0m
[32m| **Quote** | “NIA SBIR funding ceilings for FY2026 are up to $700,000 for Phase I (2‑year project) and up to $3 million for Phase II (3‑year project).” ([NIA SBIR](https://www.nia.nih.gov/research/sbir)) |

